|name3 = Racquet Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Teal Egg: N105''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Racquet Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Racquet Cat sounds pretty terrible with her niche since most [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies are ranged, however, if used properly, she can be helpful in certain situations, like pairing her with [[:Category:Sniper-class Cats|snipers]] like [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]] or [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] to help her push melee Aliens consistently without the threat of enemy backliners eliminating your whole team. She is viable against [[Star Peng]], [[Mesocosmocyclone]] and [[Cyberhorn]] with her fast, piercing attacks. While having Behemoth Slayer, the only viable Alien-Behemoth enemy she is useful against is [[Crustaceous Scissorex]] since [[Suidae Piggicus]] and [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] are immune to Knockback. But her expensive evolution requirements mean she may not worth your Behemoth Stones unless you need something that can push Aliens away.

